 "notes": {
  "5063:2508": "the parade moves down a city street and a wide avenue; a learner may read highway as any big road",
  "7264:6022": "bare word threshold = the sill of a doorway; she forces the bakery door open and stands at its threshold",
  "5372:2130": "he is cleaning a terrace whose tiles are wet; washing the terrace is arguable",
  "5372:6058": "same as washing: cleaning wet tiles, could be read as washing the terrace",
  "5372:5458": "bare word pants = trousers in everyday use; he wears shorts, arguable",
  "4171:755": "two yellow chicks are shown next to each other beside a bamboo tube",
  "5663:1588": "a man in a vest throws a hard punch in a gym; his arm muscles are visible and at work",
  "5663:1159": "a partner holds the bag and says 'Good. Again.'; reads like a boxing class / training lesson",
  "4732:5191": "bare 'fix' also means fasten: he fixes rails and posts in place with a drill; also looks like repair work",
  "4732:2684": "man with drill, mallet and level working on a fence; a learner could take it as a repair",
  "4732:1764": "a string line is pegged along the fence; string vs rope is arguable",
  "328:1745": "she talks through cooking steps ('Smash, skins off'); the clip reads like a recipe",
  "524:4916": "bare word alarm also means sudden fear or worry, a near-synonym of the key word panic",
  "5649:1729": "winner's podium implies a contest just won; race is arguable although nothing fast is shown",
  "156:1297": "the runner's face is in shot, so his eyes are visible though not the focus",
  "156:1610": "the runner's face is in shot, so his nose is visible though not the focus",
  "4173:3858": "everyday sense 'look after': the hen carries and protects her chicks under her wings"
 }
